From dc0604ad11194294e65847f39b7b2bd1942eaebb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Cueto <crcueto25@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:06:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D4b: DuDe frees the chains of each approximation pass

PATCH(dude-4b). approximate() (poly_approx.cpp) creates a c_chain with
new for each segment of a pass; the chains link to each other (pre,
next) and were never freed. They are deleted at the end of each pass,
after approximate(chains, new_approx), which is their last use.
LeakSanitizer, H-03 test alone: 1,066,400 B / 7,600 allocations before,
935,200 B / 5,550 after. DudeReference unchanged (own process and whole
program); no ASan or UBSan report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/poly_approx.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/poly_approx.cpp b/src/poly_approx.cpp
index 4ec3209..6b9ff7b 100644
--- a/src/poly_approx.cpp
+++ b/src/poly_approx.cpp
@@ -294,6 +294,10 @@ void approximate(const c_plyline &plyline, double tau,
     // approximate
     float error = approximate(chains, new_approx);
     approx = new_approx;
+    // PATCH(dude-4b): the chains of this pass (new c_chain, linked to each
+    // other) were never freed; nothing uses them after approximate()
+    for (size_t c = 0; c < chains.size(); c++)
+      delete chains[c];
     if (error < tau)
       break;
   } while (true);
